### Key design decisions

- **Two-phase parse/execute**: All options (including those after operands) are collected before any filesystem mutation, per the requirement.
- **`mkdir_parents`** splits the path on `/`, filters out empty strings (repeated slashes) and `.` components, then walks components left-to-right. Each component is either accepted (existing dir or symlink-to-dir) or created (doesn't exist). Non-directory existing components cause a `Not a directory` error referencing the full operand.
- **Intermediate permission guarantee**: After creating an intermediate component, if owner `wx` bits are missing (due to an unusual umask), they are restored via `chmod`. The final component uses the plain umask-derived mode.
- **Error messages** use `OSError.strerror` (the C library's `strerror`), which on Linux produces the exact same wording as GNU 9.11 for all relevant errnos.
- **No external calls, no subprocesses, no ctypes** — pure standard library `os` module syscalls.
